      prompt: `At December 31, Year 1, Gasp Co.'s allowance for uncollectible accounts had a credit balance of $30,000. During Year 2, Gasp wrote off uncollectible accounts of $45,000. At December 31, Year 2, an aging of the accounts receivable indicated that $50,000 of the receivables may be uncollectible. What amount of bad debt expense should Gasp recognize during Year 2?`,
